WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.480
Before you

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:00.880
record a

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:01.840
bug fix,

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:02.400
check what

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.040
will actually

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:03.440
go into

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.640
the next commit.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.840
Git status gives

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:06.160
you that

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:06.800
report,

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:07.440
including your

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.440
current branch.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.960
Imagine three changes,

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:11.440
a bug

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.040
fix already staged,

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.040
an edited note

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.280
still unstaged,

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:15.520
and a

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:16.680
new sketch Git

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:17.920
is not tracking.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.680
Status separates those three

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.520
situations.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.080
The staged

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:22.560
fix is

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.120
prepared for

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.160
the next commit.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:24.720
The note

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:25.520
and sketch

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:26.080
are outside

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:26.480
the next

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.040
commit,

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:27.520
and one

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:28.080
file can

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:28.640
appear in

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.680
both staged and

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.200
unstaged changes if you

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:31.680
edit it

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.000
again after staging.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.120
Status only reports

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:36.000
the situation.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:36.480
It does

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.120
not stage

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:37.760
your work.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:38.160
Read it

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.280
before committing so

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:39.600
you know

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.000
what is

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:40.640
prepared and

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.200
what still

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.320
needs a decision.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:42.880
That helps

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:43.360
you notice

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:43.920
a missing

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:44.560
file before

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:45.040
you record

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:45.720
the change.
